# Defend the Rider, second mode: the Pilot token "saddles Mounts ... as though its power were 2 greater", so its 1 power
# counts as 3 (CR 702.171a). Turn 1: with only Mother of Runes (power 1) the Caustic Bronco (Saddle 3) cannot be saddled
# (the refusal); after Defend the Rider makes a Pilot, the Pilot alone saddles it (summoning sickness does not matter:
# CR 702.171a taps creatures as a cost, not a {T} ability), and the Bronco is saddled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Caustic Bronco
Mother of Runes
Defend the Rider
Forest
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Caustic Bronco.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
! Bot1.Battlefield.Caustic Bronco.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Defend the Rider.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Create a 1/1 colorless Pilot creature token with "This token saddles Mounts and crews Vehicles as though its power were 2 greater.")
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Pilot Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Caustic Bronco.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Pilot Token)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Caustic Bronco.Saddled = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Pilot Token.Tapped = True
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Tapped = False
